   "flags": {},
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "widgets_values": [
    "## pixel-art.json\n\nPixel art (game-ready sprites)\n\n**Does:** SDXL + `pixel-art-xl` LoRA (RealVisXL, strength 1.0) at **1024²** -> `ImageScale` **nearest /16** = 64x64, then a palette pass (`PixelArtDetectorToImage`, 16 colours). Run it at 1024²: at 512² the frames come out far too tight.\n**Downscale by NEAREST with the model's KNOWN factor** (16 here). Never trust the detector's auto-detect - it mis-detects, and it is not idempotent, so only ever feed it the generation-sized image.\n**Want the flat retro look instead?** Switch the checkpoint to `RetroDiffusion24x-64xModel` at **512²**, 20 steps, cfg 9.5, and divide by **8** (its grid is 8 px at 512²). That model is **non-commercial**; `pixel-art-xl` is OpenRAIL, which is why this is the shipped arm.\n**Already have a picture?** `pixel-art-convert.json` pixelises and palettises an existing image to a chosen palette instead of generating one.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S10** in `HOWTO.md`  ·  Why it is this way: **E5/E5b/E5f** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "properties": {},
   "order": 0
  }
